claim:
V1-1 leaves the cursor on the empty line after a final newline. That happens after `o<Esc>` on a last line with no final newline, `A<CR><Esc>`, or typing lines into a new buffer. From there:
- `0`, `^` and `$` move the cursor to the last character of the line above;
- `}` moves up instead of signalling;
- `u` of a session typed on that line also leaves it.
Evil and Vim stay on the line. This is outside the "last line" deviation, which only stops motions from reaching that line.

